You must submit a `development_result` artifact before ending the phase: a markdown document with frontmatter `type: development_result` and `status: completed|partial|failed`. `status: completed` means the entire plan is done: every required plan item must be implemented or have a proven disposition that preserves every request criterion. Completing only some items is incremental progress, not completion. A completed result then has `## Summary` (exactly one item), `## Files Changed` (one item per file), and the proof sections below. Each proof item's bracketed ID is the reference; the item text is the evidence.

**Proof IDs in `## Plan Items Proven` are shape-independent.** A bracketed ID in `## Plan Items Proven` may be any stable reference the plan actually uses — a step ID (`S-N`), a work-unit ID, a prose-plan ID (`plan`), a subplan heading, or any other anchor the developer chose. The validator never rejects a plan-item ID solely for not matching a plan-parsed ID; on plan items it only rejects duplicate IDs and a missing or unknown `Disposition`. A missing `Rationale` is rejected only for `adapted` / `not_applicable` / `blocked` items — completed items do not. When a plan item's proof text claims the UI work, its proof must also cite a design verdict id and capture handles — judged from the item's proof text, never from the bracketed reference label, so a relabeled reference never changes acceptance. Coverage of the plan's intent is now enforced through the development analysis feedback loop (U-2), not by exact ID matching here. `## Analysis Items Addressed` IDs are not shape-independent: each must match the prior analysis's stable finding ID exactly, and a missing or unknown analysis finding ID fails proof validation.

**## Plan Items Proven** (required when the execution plan has steps, including steps grouped into named subplans, or when the plan explicitly uses `## Work Units` / `## Parallel Plan`): one `- [<ID>] <proof>` item per work unit, per plan step, or per section of the plan. The bracketed ID matches whatever the plan or work-unit declares — a stable step ID, a work-unit bracket ID, a prose-plan ID, or a subplan / section heading. Add an indented `Disposition: completed|adapted|not_applicable|blocked` field and an indented `Rationale:` for `adapted`, `not_applicable`, or `blocked`. The proof cites concrete, reproducible evidence. A completed artifact cannot contain `blocked`; submit a partial result instead.

For `adapted`, identify the inaccurate route and explain how the changed route preserves the intended outcome. For `not_applicable`, identify the plan assumption, cite fresh contradictory or already-satisfied evidence at a reproducible location or command, and explain why no request criterion loses coverage. Difficulty, elapsed time, an unrelated green check, or speculation is not a valid rationale.

**## Analysis Items Addressed** (required when ANALYSIS FEEDBACK exists): one `- [<ID>] <proof>` item per localized `What Came Up Short` finding from the prior analysis artifact, where the ID matches that entry's stable ID (e.g. `DA-001`) and the proof cites how it was resolved.

Each proof ID must be distinct — duplicates fail validation. Every requirement above applies to `status: completed`. `partial` and `failed` are accepted at any point, but they are last-resort outcomes, not shortcuts. The rule for when each is permitted lives in `shared/_no_exemption_for_failures.j2` — refer to it before deciding between `completed`, `partial`, or `failed`. Both statuses close this developer attempt and flow to independent analysis; neither decides whether the run ends. The submitted partial or failed artifact must still include the evidence, remaining work, external action required, and why no in-scope developer action can complete it. After submitting `partial`, call `declare_complete` once with `partial_reason` set to that literal impossibility; no second confirmation call is required.

**## Unplanned Work** (optional, any status): required work the plan omitted or mid-phase discoveries. Use one `- [UW-N]` bullet per item, naming the request criterion, the action taken and changed paths, a stable `path:line` anchor, and reproducible proof (command plus observed result, or a cited source location). Complete required in-scope work now; a missing plan step is not a reason to defer it. These entries supplement `## Plan Items Proven` and `## Analysis Items Addressed`, never replace them. UW IDs identify discoveries, not plan-step references, and are not routed to plan proof validation. For an unresolved external blocker, state the evidence and external action required honestly.
